### Refresh numbered shortcut cue tracking when the hosted list changes

**Severity:** `medium`

The cue host is selected from the current list layout, but this only refreshes while cues are already visible. If the page switches between list/grid layout or swaps in a populated nested list before access-key mode is active, the cue canvas and UIA accelerator metadata can remain wired to the old host. Track the view model lifecycle while loaded and queue an update whenever the layout changes.

```suggestion
            if (@this._isLoaded)
            {
                @this.EnsureNumberedShortcutCueTracking();
                @this.QueueNumberedShortcutCueUpdate();
            }
```

### Recompute accelerator assignments when item interactivity changes

**Severity:** `medium`

The shortcut numbers skip non-interactive items, but the current cue metadata is only recomputed on full item updates. If an item toggles `IsInteractive` while the filtered collection stays the same, the visible cue numbers and automation accelerators can point at stale items. Subscribe to filtered collection changes and each visible item's `PropertyChanged`, then queue a cue update when `IsInteractive` changes; gate those subscriptions to views with `ShowNumberedShortcutCues` enabled so parameter lists do not pay the tracking cost.

```suggestion
                page.ItemsUpdated += @this.Page_ItemsUpdated;
                page.PropertyChanged += @this.ViewModel_PropertyChanged;
                if (@this.ShowNumberedShortcutCues)
                {
                    page.FilteredItems.CollectionChanged += @this.FilteredItems_CollectionChanged;
                    @this.RefreshNumberedShortcutItemTracking();
                }
```
